WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.132 --> 00:00:02.801
-Jake Gyllenhaal.
It's good to see you, buddy.

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:04.937
You seem kind of down.

00:00:04.937 --> 00:00:07.040
Everything alright?
-Yeah, no, everything is okay.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.307
[ Laughter ]

00:00:08.307 --> 00:00:09.876
-Wow. Oh, my goodness.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:12.311
-It's kind of been a tough week.

00:00:12.311 --> 00:00:13.546
-Really?

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:16.049
-Had to cut my dog's balls off.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:19.151
[ Laughter ]

00:00:19.151 --> 00:00:22.856
-You, you -- you yourself?

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:25.791
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:28.061
-I would've liked to, probably.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.329
-Because you love your dog.

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:30.329
-But a professional
should do that.

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:32.565
-You had a professional do it.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.801
That's a tough thing to do.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.871
-Yeah. Sorry to bring it down.
It's just --

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.539
-No, they're having a good time.
They're laughing.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:41.106
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.106 --> 00:00:42.675
They're actually having
a good time with this.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:45.478
-Maybe some of you empathize --
I mean, with your dogs.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:48.747
With your dogs.
-Wait, but is it a puppy?

00:00:48.747 --> 00:00:50.717
-No, he's actually
seven years old.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.185
-Whoa.
-Yeah, I know.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.786
Well, I should explain.

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:57.857
He had hip problems when he was
a baby, so they told me

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.826
instead of giving him surgery
and have him go through pain

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:03.730
when he was a little puppy,
that I should keep him intact,

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:08.668
and that the muscles --
that the testosterone would --

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:09.902
the muscles around his hips,

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:11.671
the testosterone would help
build stronger.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:12.972
It's a holistic approach, right?

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:16.742
-Of course. Sure, sure, sure.
-And I said, "Okay."

00:01:16.742 --> 00:01:18.811
But then, as he's gotten
a little bit older,

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:22.648
he's seven years old now, his
prostate has become a problem.

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:26.285
So they suggested that I get him
neutered for health reasons.

00:01:26.285 --> 00:01:29.722
And so, I said, "Okay, good.
That needs to happen."

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.124
-Absolutely, you've got to
take care of the dog.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:37.497
-Yeah, so, I was about to,
and then I was looking at

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.131
some photographs on the Internet

00:01:39.131 --> 00:01:41.434
of neutered dogs
of an older age.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.002
-You've done this for years.

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.137
-Well, yeah, my doctor
had suggested that

00:01:45.137 --> 00:01:47.206
maybe he should get Neuticles.

00:01:47.206 --> 00:01:49.142
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:50.943
Do you know what those are?

00:01:50.943 --> 00:01:52.879
-No, I could guess, maybe.

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.614
-They're prosthetic testicles.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:58.818
[ Laughter ]
So, I said, "No."

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:00.486
-Of course, yeah.
-Of course.

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:02.188
And then I was like,
"Well, what do they look like?"

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:04.023
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:07.327
-Dude, you can get in trouble
for Googling stuff like that.

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:09.696
-What I saw was what happens

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:11.097
with a dog
when they don't have them.

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:12.866
And it's just
an empty sack of --

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:15.234
-Alright, Jake, thanks.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:19.772
-So I ended up calling my doctor
the night before surgery

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:22.574
and saying, "Can we get these
things, these Neuticles?"

00:02:22.574 --> 00:02:23.910
Can we get them stat?"

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.578
Like they say on "E.R."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.180
-You did not say "stat."
-I did.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.249
I called her immediately.
I said, "Can we get them stat?"

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:32.218
And she said, "You're going to
have to wait." So I waited.

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:34.053
-Even though you used
the correct medical term?

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:35.955
-Yeah.
-Yeah. You cannot get them stat.

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:41.026
-Stat. And I had to figure out
what size they were.

00:02:41.026 --> 00:02:43.329
-No, this is insane now.
No, this is insane.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:44.463
[ Laughter ]
-But it's true.

00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:46.198
-Well, you let the dog choose.

00:02:46.198 --> 00:02:49.101
-The dog has --
He's a German Shepherd.

00:02:49.101 --> 00:02:52.005
He has German Shepherd-size
testicles.

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:53.239
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:55.742
Anyway, long story short,
he has Neuticles.

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:57.076
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.076 --> 00:03:01.080
-And are the Neuticles --
what dog --

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.183
What breed did you go with
for the Neuticles?

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:06.252
-Well, obviously
the Chihuahua's.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:09.522
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:11.624
No, come on. No, no.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:13.058
Gorilla. Gorilla.

00:03:13.058 --> 00:03:15.895
-Gorilla.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:18.697
Unbelievable.
Well, the dog is healthy.

00:03:18.697 --> 00:03:21.167
-He's great. He's fine.
He's healthy. He's happy.

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:23.503
He has no recollection
whatsoever.

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:24.870
-That's what we wanted.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:27.373
-I'm sorry. I didn't mean
to bring you all down.

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.475
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:32.144
Yeah. Yeah.
-I love seeing you.

00:03:32.144 --> 00:03:34.180
I do want to say this
before we get into anything,

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:38.251
because I was with my friend
maybe about a month ago,

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:40.018
we're just playing
song for song.

00:03:40.018 --> 00:03:42.422
Just going song for --
You get a song, I get a song.

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:44.023
Doesn't have to be anything.

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:46.859
And he played me this song,

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:48.561
"Sunday in the Park
with George."

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:50.729
I think the name of
the song is "Sunday."

00:03:50.729 --> 00:03:53.165
And he played it and I was like,
"Love this."

00:03:53.165 --> 00:03:54.534
I go, "Who is this?"

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:56.401
He goes, "It's Jake Gyllenhaal."

00:03:56.401 --> 00:03:59.738
And I was like -- Dude, you are
phenomenal in that play.

00:03:59.738 --> 00:04:01.107
-Oh, thanks, man.
-You got a voice.

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:03.609
Oh, my gosh. Not just good.

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:05.644
Great. Fantastic.

00:04:05.644 --> 00:04:07.079
And I know that you can sing,

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:08.748
and we've done bits on the show
so many times.

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:11.651
But man, oh, man, you knocked
that one out of the park, buddy.

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:13.419
-Well, it's a pretty incredible
show.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:14.987
We did it on Broadway,
and then we were about

00:04:14.987 --> 00:04:18.891
to go do it in London, and then
the worldwide pandemic hit,

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.326
and then we had to cancel.

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:23.696
-Does it feel good that you're
on -- I mean, you're on Spotify.

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:25.297
-Yeah.
-That's cool.

00:04:25.297 --> 00:04:27.800
-No, it is super cool.
My name doesn't even fit.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.502
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:31.670
-It scrolls past.
-It was a whole cast.

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:34.707
They just, like --
"Let's just leave his name off."

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:37.009
-But I saw you at the Tonys,
by the way.

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:38.477
You got nominated for a Tony.

00:04:38.477 --> 00:04:40.146
Look at this. Come on.
It's Jake Gyllenhaal.

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:42.281
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:44.683
You look great.
-Thank you.

00:04:44.683 --> 00:04:46.118
-Everyone was talking about --

00:04:46.118 --> 00:04:48.821
You had a baby pink tux
that people were talking about.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.890
-Baby pink, yeah.
-Baby pink. People loved it.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.626
-It was a really,
nice, soft thing.

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.261
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:57.696
"GQ" said you won the night.

00:04:57.696 --> 00:04:59.465
Look at that.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:01.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That's nice.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:04.370
-It's nice to see
Broadway is back.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.038
-Oh, it's so great.
-How did it feel?

00:05:06.038 --> 00:05:07.707
What was the energy like?
-It's so great.

00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:09.175
It's wonderful.
I mean, it's like --

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:10.810
To think of everything that
we've been through,

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:13.312
particularly Broadway and
everyone who works on Broadway,

00:05:13.312 --> 00:05:16.282
to come back, to feel like we
actually, probably,

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:19.084
are going to last this through
and stay

00:05:19.084 --> 00:05:21.620
and to see an audience here --
just a live audience.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:24.457
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:26.059
-It's the best.
-It's the best.

